      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start and definitely sounds professional. \n\ni just checked the sample profiles from other successful applicants and most of them have way higher keyword density than this. i think the recruiter might actually be looking for a really strong emphasis on these values to filter through the thousands of apps they get. \n\ncan you try to rewrite it to make the \"value alignment\" much more prominent? i still want it to be a coherent letter, but try to weave those specific terms in more frequently throughout the body paragraphs so the score is significantly higher. i really need that score to be high so i don't get filtered out immediately.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
